        "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x}$ given that $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}={y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}.$",
        "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202y\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}+2{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y} \\\\  & =2y(y+1){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
